==Latin==

===Etymology===
See {{m|la|dominor}}.

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|dominō}}

# {{lb|la|rare}} I [[rule]], [[control]]; I [[win]], [[overcome]]; {{synonym of|la|dominor|nocap=1}}
#: {{syn|la|devinco|supero|conquesto|subigo|vinco|profligo|caedo|pello|domo}}

====Usage notes====
This is a regularised active form of the deponent verb {{m|la|dominor}}, which is much more common. The consequence of this situation is that {{m|la|dominor}} can occasionally mean "I am ruled" as well as the more usual sense "I rule".

